  "body": "Move the web API to a dedicated Hetzner CPX12 at about $16.79/month with backups and IPv4, replacing a known Fly production baseline of about $23.56/month. Fly billing blocks both release creation and Machine updates; the operator explicitly approved a web-first cutover with downtime for older mobile installs until updated.\n\nAdds isolated restore and production Compose configurations, pinned-image preparation using the existing release source/migration/recovery guards, daily logical backups, and a transactional update of TDF-owned asset/radio URLs. The frontend fallback uses `https://api.tdfrecords.net`. Production writer fencing, a fresh final restore, provider callback changes, and the frontend environment switch remain cutover operations; the current public Hetzner edge exposes only health/version.\n\nValidation: production-copy restore on PostgreSQL 17 with vector 0.8.1; all 115 registered migrations and schema verification; recovery-image drill and return to the exact target; 82 release tests; 5 API-base tests; repository quality gate; 64/64 concurrent feed requests with CORS and outbound isolation; all 37 referenced migrated asset files present. The URL update changed 34 assets, 3 event images and 1 radio URL; its second run changed no rows. Private backups and credentials are excluded from this PR. Detailed evidence and remaining cutover gates are in `ops/hetzner/`.\n\nTradeoff: this consolidates onto one host and reduces the previous API's regional redundancy. Existing Fly charges continue until superseded resources are deliberately retired. Event PRs #460/#463/#464 are separate.\n",
